General Description of Project Progress
Since Progress Report #1, we completed end-to-end gameplay and significantly expanded
scope with distributed features, richer combat mechanics, and usability improvements.

1. End-to-End Distributed Gameplay Completed
- Full host/join battle flow is implemented and stable.
- Armies and shared RNG seed are exchanged across nodes.
- Name exchange between peers is implemented so both terminals display real player names.
- Graceful disconnect handling is implemented (including SIGINT cleanup).
- Rematch negotiation is fully integrated after each match.

2. Expanded Distributed Features
- Node discovery mode is added via a discovery list file:
  --join-any <nodes_file> <port>
  This lets a client attempt multiple candidate hosts in sequence.
- Third-node spectator support is added with UDP:
  --spectator-listen <port> (observer node)
  --spectator <host> <port> (battle nodes stream live logs)
- This enables a 3-node demo setup on linprog (host, joiner, observer).

3. Battle Engine Enhancements
- AI target selection is now role-aware (not only random targeting).
  Example behavior includes prioritizing high-impact enemy units and weaker targets.
- Match environment complexity was introduced:
  - Random weather per match (Clear, Rain, Fog, Storm, Heatwave)
  - Random map pool per match (Plains, Urban, Mountains, Coastal, Ruins)
  - Dynamic world events:
    - EMP disruption round (missile/artillery jamming)
    - Third-party drone intervention round (neutral damage to both armies)
- Between rounds, each player now provides input (press Enter) before continuing.
  This adds interactive pacing during combat.

4. Software Architecture and Organization
- New modules were added to keep features organized:
  - ai_strategy.cpp/.h: AI target selection behavior
  - discovery.cpp/.h: node discovery join logic
  - spectator.cpp/.h: observer streaming/listener mode
  - battle_environment.cpp/.h: weather/map/event mechanics
- Existing modules were updated:
  - main.cpp: integrated discovery, spectator, rematch, and name exchange
  - battle.cpp: environment effects and interactive round pacing
  - protocol.cpp/.h: additional protocol message support
  - README.md: updated run instructions and feature documentation

5. Build and Validation
- Build remains Makefile-driven and compiles cleanly.
- Current executable supports:
  - host mode
  - join mode
  - auto-discovery join mode
  - spectator listen mode
  - spectator streaming from active players
- Manual testing has been performed for:
  - host/join connectivity
  - spectator path
  - rematch flow
  - environment/event round behavior

